# Build artifacts
_build/
*.o
*.elf
*.hex
*.map

# ...except the bootloader binary, which is SHIPPED, not built: users cannot build
# it themselves, so Tools > Burn Bootloader flashes this committed file. It is
# reproducible from the C sources beside it via _build/build_bootloader.sh.
# make-release.sh refuses to package an untracked file, so without this negation a
# release would fail rather than silently ship a bootloader-less platform.
!arduino-platform/microchip/dspic33ck/bootloaders/**/*.hex
*.lst
*.d

# Arduino IDE cache/build
sketches/

# MPLAB X project files
nbproject/
*.X/
MPLABXLog.xml
**/MPLABXLog.xml

# Archives (can be regenerated)
*.zip
*.tar.bz2

# IDE and editor files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Test binaries
test_led/*.elf
test_led/*.hex

# OS files
.DS_Store

# Temporary/scratch files
*.tmp
*.bak

# Claude Code memory (local only)
.claude/

# Copyrighted PDFs (don't redistribute)
*.pdf

# Python bytecode. This lands INSIDE the shipped platform tree -- importing
# tools/serial_upload.py, which _build/bootloader_check.sh does to read its
# constants, creates tools/__pycache__/ next to it. make-release.sh refuses to
# ship untracked files, so it would not reach a release, but it should not be
# committed and should not clutter a test install either.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

